    VALUES (NULL, $q$Machining - Plunging$q$, 'process', 'single', false, true, true, $q$Plunging a turned groove with a grooving insert, as the Machining calculator workbook's Cutoff sheet times a radial plunge: n = 1000 v / (pi D) at the groove's diameter, capped at the machine's spindle limit; plunges = the groove's width over the insert's, rounded up; time = plunges x (groove depth + 10 mm) / (feed x n), rounded up to whole seconds a groove. The insert is as wide as the groove, at most the widest of the grooving table; its cutting speed and feed are the material's rows of tblGrooving (migration 746, nearest hardness within the material's cut-code family, as Parting reads its part-off inserts), the feed read between the 1.75 mm and 8 mm inserts in proportion to the insert's width (the 1.75 mm row's feed for a narrower one). The groove's diameter, depth and width are the CAD's (its major diameter, and the depth and chord width of its round profile). Tool price and life from the workbook's Cutoff sheet (the insert holder).$q$)
    RETURNING id INTO v_id;
  ELSE
    UPDATE public.calculators SET description = $q$Plunging a turned groove with a grooving insert, as the Machining calculator workbook's Cutoff sheet times a radial plunge: n = 1000 v / (pi D) at the groove's diameter, capped at the machine's spindle limit; plunges = the groove's width over the insert's, rounded up; time = plunges x (groove depth + 10 mm) / (feed x n), rounded up to whole seconds a groove. The insert is as wide as the groove, at most the widest of the grooving table; its cutting speed and feed are the material's rows of tblGrooving (migration 746, nearest hardness within the material's cut-code family, as Parting reads its part-off inserts), the feed read between the 1.75 mm and 8 mm inserts in proportion to the insert's width (the 1.75 mm row's feed for a narrower one). The groove's diameter, depth and width are the CAD's (its major diameter, and the depth and chord width of its round profile). Tool price and life from the workbook's Cutoff sheet (the insert holder).$q$, updated_at = now() WHERE id = v_id;
  END IF;

